The following is a walkthrough on how to configure EVPN through BGP on a Dell Enterprise Sonic device:

## 1. Configure BGP

### Loopback Interfaces

Configure a loopback interface on each of the switches in the network, and assign it an IP address.

```
interface loopback0
ip address 10.0.0.1/32
```

### Inter-Link Connections

Configure /31 addresses for links between the spine and TORs which will facilitate BGP traffic.

```
# Spine
interface eth1/1
ip address 10.99.0.2/31

# Tor
interface eth1/1
ip address 10.99.0.3/31
```

### BGP Configuration

Configure BGP between Spine and TOR switches, where each layer of the network uses it's own AS and leverages eBGP.

```
# spine
route bgp 65000
  router-id $LOOPBACK_ADDRESS

  neighbor 10.99.0.3
    remote-as 65001

    address-famil ipv4 unicast
      activate

    address-family l2vpn evpn
      activate
```

## 2. VXLAN

### Anycast Gateways

For VLANs being mapped across the VXLAN network, anycast addresses can act as distributed gateways on each leaf switch in the fabric. Servers then route traffic to their directly connected leaf switch which handles the routing from there.

The gateway MAC and IP is advertised with the Default Gateway Extended Community falg over the EVPN network, signalling to other leaf switches that it is a distributed gateway.

